   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Your Kubernetes Job is broken, and it keeps retrying for minutes?"
  },
  {
   "id": "bug",
   "text": "Most devs never set this."
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "text": "By default, backoff limit is six. Failed pods are recreated with an exponential delay, ten, twenty, forty seconds, capped at ten minutes."
  },
  {
   "id": "fix",
   "text": "Set a lower backoff limit to fail fast, and add active deadline seconds to cap the total runtime. The deadline wins over retries."
  },
  {
   "id": "bait",
   "text": "Fail fast or retry more? Comment which one you pick."
  },
  {
